# Shell scripts run on Linux and the Steam Deck, where a carriage return at the end of a
# line breaks them ("bash\r: No such file or directory"). This machine checks files out
# with Windows line endings, so the scripts have to be pinned to LF here or they would
# ship broken.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Batch files are the other way round. cmd.exe finds a label by reading the file in
# 512-byte blocks, and with bare LF line endings it can land part way through a line and
# jump to the wrong place, or not find the label at all. They are stored with LF like
# everything else, but checked out - and so packaged and uploaded - with CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
